course: dictionary
lesson: 8651
title: Searing: very hot, very strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Searing is an adjective that means extremely hot, hot enough to burn. «The searing heat made the road shimmer in the desert.» The word searing tells you how strong the heat is, so you can picture a burning sun.
explain: The same word can describe strong feelings too. «A searing pain shot up his leg» means the pain was sudden, sharp and very strong. «She gave him a searing look» means a harsh, angry look. Check the words around it: pain, look and heat each show which meaning fits.
explain: Searing can also be a verb, sear. Chefs sear meat by cooking its outside quickly in a very hot pan until it turns brown. To check, swap in the meaning: "cooking the outside quickly at a very high heat" must still make sense in the sentence.
fact: Searing means extremely hot, hot enough to burn.
fact: Searing pain is sudden, sharp and very strong.
fact: Searing words or criticism are very harsh and strong.
fact: As a verb, sear means to brown the outside of meat quickly in a very hot pan, or to burn a surface.
fact: Searing meat does not seal in the juices: seared meat loses as much moisture as unseared meat, but browning adds flavour.
exercise: «The searing heat made the road shimmer.» What does searing mean here? | Quiet and gentle | Very slow | Cold and wet | *Extremely hot, hot enough to burn
exercise: «Her searing look made him go quiet.» What does searing suggest? | Happy and kind | Pale and cold | Sleepy and tired | *Very harsh and angry
exercise: Chef Tom says, «Sear the steak in the hot pan for two minutes.» What does sear mean? | Soak it in cold water | *Cook the outside quickly at a high heat until brown | Cut it into thin slices | Freeze it solid in the fridge
test: «A searing pain shot through his leg after the fall.» What does searing mean here? | *Sudden, sharp and very strong | Dull and gentle | Cold and numb | Slow and steady
test: Does searing meat seal in the juices? | No, it makes the meat frozen | Yes, it locks them in completely | Yes, it makes the meat cold | *No, seared meat loses as much moisture as unseared meat, but browning adds flavour
exam: «Searing heat can cause burns, so stay in the shade and drink water.» What is a safe thing to do in searing heat? | *Stay in the shade and drink water | Wear no hat and no water | Sit in the sun all day | Run hard without a break
